@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] native-git-owner-authority
The helper MUST execute only trusted caller-supplied absolute executables and
argument vectors without a shell, with no setuid or file capabilities. Its stdout
is private command output, never diagnostics. It MUST emit no argv, paths,
credentials or raw native errors as diagnostics.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery;capacity] native-git-lifetime
Caller EOF, command timeout, output overflow and normal command exit MUST kill
and reap the private process group before releasing repository/admission locks.
At most eight native commands may own global admission slots. Stable lock inodes
MUST NOT be unlinked, and descendants MUST retain locks until they terminate.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] native-git-owner-proof
Native owner-death, timeout, output bounds, contention and successor admission
MUST have generated tests with independent process and lock witnesses. Local
process checks MUST NOT establish remote TLS, physical quotas or fleet service
acceptance.
